{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "RUP \"Rational Unified Process\"", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Rational Unified Process. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.   Talk about particular topics related to sofware programming.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Be Used to + Ing in Affirmative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><strong>Be used to</strong></span> is an expression to talk about something that is familiar to us or that is not unusual.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The structure for this expression is: </br></br> <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + be used to + verb (ing form) + complement</div></br></br>  Example: </br>   <span class=\"italic\"> I'<b>m used to</b> following the different stages of program development. </span></br></br>  Notice that the verb after <b>be used to</b> goes in the <strong>gerund form</strong> (ing) and the <strong>verb to be</strong> is conjugated in accordance with the subject</strong> (am, is, are).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You know I'm used to doing things on my own, but I don't know what to do. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm used to working with RUP. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm used to developing software in a different way. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm very used to working on this phase, but I still have to learn much more about it.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Not Only--- but (Also) ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The construction<strong> not only\u2026but (also)</strong> is a conjunction used to present two related pieces of information.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we want to present two pieces of information together, and one of them is surprising or somehow unexpected, we used the structure <strong>not only\u2026but (also).</strong> </br></br>  The first piece of information always goes right after <strong>not only </strong>and the second (and unexpected) piece of information goes after <strong>but (also)</strong>:</br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\"> The developer <b>not only</b> creates the application design <b>but also</b> the source code.  </span></br></br>  Notice that the main verb goes in the affirmative form and is not repeated in the second part of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Well, it means that this tool not only combines the procedural aspects of development with other components but also includes them within a unifying network. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In the inception phase, you not only have the chance to define the scope of the project but also to define its business case.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "architectural foundation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "set of principal design decisions about the system", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  During the elaboration phase, my favorite, you analyze the project's needs in detail, and define the architectural foundation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "business case", "type": "name"}, {"content": "argument intended to convince a decision maker to agree with some kind of action", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the inception phase, you not only have the chance to define the scope of the project but also to define its business case.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "guideline ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "guide or indication for any given course of action", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's like an online instructor that gives you templates, guidelines, and examples of program development.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "inception", "type": "name"}, {"content": "initial stage of a developmental procedure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the inception phase, you not only have the chance to define the scope of the project but also to define its business case.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "iteration ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a method in which a continuation of approximations, each building on the one preceding, is used to achieve a desired degree of accuracy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  This process divides steps into certain separate iterations that must satisfy defined criteria before the next phase initiates.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob04aud05", "type": 