P, and I don't even know what that is. I'm so going to fail this course!</br>\n<strong>Sue:</strong> You found the right person; I'm used to working with RUP. </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> Cool. So, let's start. What's RUP?</br>", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "29000", "text": "<strong>Sue:</strong> RUP, or Rational Unified Process, is an object-oriented and web-enabled methodology. It's like an online instructor that gives you templates, guidelines, and examples of program development. </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> Sounds interesting! I heard it is a comprehensive software engineering tool. But, what does it mean?</br>\n<strong>Sue:</strong> Well, it means that this tool not only combines the procedural aspects of development with other components but also includes them within a unifying network. </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> I see. I'm used to developing software in a different way. </br>\n<strong>Sue:</strong> Don't worry! RUP should show you the way through some phases of development.", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "72600", "text": "<strong>Peter:</strong> Phases?</br>\n<strong>Sue:</strong> That's right. This process divides steps into certain separate iterations that must satisfy defined criteria before the next phase initiates. In the inception phase, you not only have the chance to define the scope of the project but also to define its business case. During the elaboration phase, my favorite, you analyze the project's needs in detail, and define the architectural foundation. Then, during the construction phase, you create the application design and source code. I'm very used to working on this phase, but I still have to learn much more about it. Finally, in the transition phase, you deliver the system to users. </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> Now, I have a better picture. Thanks a lot, Sue!</br>\n<strong>Sue:</strong> No problem!", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le03ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}